research/level9-judge.jsonl:57:{"id":"fs-arbitrary-product-of-open-sets-is-open","model":"z-ai/glm-5.2","keep":true,"reason":"Verified the refutation: the proof correctly shows that C = prod_k (0,1) is not open in R^N with the product topology by finding a coordinate j with O_j = R for any basic open neighbourhood O of c, constructing y in O with y_j = 2, and noting y not in C. All [L#] facts faithfully restate their cited sources: [L2] correctly combines lem-of-naturals-positive (strict increase on {1,2,...} and 1>0) with def-canonical-natural (iota(0)=0, iota(1)=1) to get strict increase on all of N; [L3] is a faithful reindexing of lem-finite-set-has-max; [L1] and [A1]-[A2] are accurate. No logical gaps or mis-citations found.","at":"2026-07-27T06:02:28.104Z"}
research/frontier-7-proof-contracts.json:6690:          "quote": "Let $p \\in \\mathbb{Q}$ with $p > 0$. For a natural number $k \\ge 1$ write\n$\\iota(k) = k \\cdot 1_{\\mathbb{R}}$ for the canonical natural, which is positive\n([[lem-of-naturals-positive]]), and write $k^{p} := \\iota(k)^{p}$ for its rational\npower ([[def-rational-power]]). Then",
