research/audit/wave1b-judge-paired.jsonl:103:{"id":"lem-of-mult-neg","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":false,"reason":"L1 misstates def-field: it calls additive-inverse uniqueness and double negation field axioms, but def-field gives only existence of inverses; its remarks defer uniqueness to lem-of-inverse-unique. Steps 3.1-3.3 and 4.1 rely on these uncited claims.","context_sha256":"5f51ccaabb3fea8afb6db7769fea69554c646e4d323a2880b1a92215790f667f","at":"2026-08-03T07:26:51.916Z"}
research/audit/wave1b-judge-paired.jsonl:109:{"id":"lem-of-inverse-unique","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":true,"reason":"Verified that the group axioms cited in L1 license each uniqueness argument and the conclusion has the required nonzero qualification for multiplicative inverses.","context_sha256":"419d6a02d9b44485c003674c78e83f00725ecf6082de04cae874a4e1e9d5c0a2","at":"2026-08-03T07:27:08.407Z"}
research/audit/wave1b-judge-paired.jsonl:121:{"id":"lem-of-inverse-positive","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":true,"reason":"Verified each step follows from the stated ordered-field and sign-rule facts; the reciprocal inequality is derived correctly.","context_sha256":"f69074eeab2079cb28440f073ea05766789e54af66c0e0869d9c50e91514926a","at":"2026-08-03T07:27:51.376Z"}
research/audit/wave1b-judge-paired.jsonl:123:{"id":"lem-of-abs-value","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":false,"reason":"Step 1.4 asserts xy = 0 when x = 0 or y = 0, but cites only L1, which is the absolute-value definition. Zero multiplication is neither stated in L1 nor established by the cited facts, so this case lacks its needed dependency.","context_sha256":"aecd5d16dbeb1e08aaa7799ea77b6647a9b62c1494a809c837945b274fdb998a","at":"2026-08-03T07:27:57.791Z"}
research/audit/wave1b-judge-paired.jsonl:124:{"id":"cor-of-reverse-triangle","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":false,"reason":"L2 attributes the claim that absolute value equals its argument or its negative to lem-of-abs-value, but that claim is not in that lemma's Statement; it comes from def-abs-value. Step 2.1 relies on this mis-cited claim.","context_sha256":"ad3986472bba0b894215140184a158e54d5a686efc7a3dfd4de71c5eb340a53d","at":"2026-08-03T07:28:03.057Z"}
research/audit/wave1b-judge-paired.jsonl:128:{"id":"lem-of-triangle-inequality","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":true,"reason":"Verified the cited bounds, nonstrict addition argument, and negation step correctly yield the triangle inequality.","context_sha256":"39a55dd1003fe17cd4c532d8c78272e493abaf9df1765adf95b69d6439a492ae","at":"2026-08-03T07:28:19.305Z"}
research/audit/wave1b-judge-paired.jsonl:129:{"id":"lem-of-square-monotone","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":false,"reason":"L3 attributes the identity that the square of the absolute value equals the original square to lem-of-abs-value, but that cited statement does not state this identity. Step 5.1 depends on this unsupported stronger fact.","context_sha256":"3d586103fac8c461de2b0a3393bceab0298605f86e8a5179b42eb32575b75633","at":"2026-08-03T07:28:23.981Z"}
research/audit/wave1b-judge-paired.jsonl:135:{"id":"lem-of-inverse-unique","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","keep":true,"reason":"The proof correctly derives uniqueness of identities and inverses from the group axioms restated in [L1]; each step is licensed by the cited facts and logically sound.","context_sha256":"419d6a02d9b44485c003674c78e83f00725ecf6082de04cae874a4e1e9d5c0a2","at":"2026-08-03T07:29:02.886Z"}
research/audit/wave1b-judge-paired.jsonl:137:{"id":"def-canonical-natural","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":false,"reason":"The remarks say lem-of-naturals-positive shows that iota carries sums and products to sums and products, but that lemma states those identities only for m,n at least 1. The unqualified claim includes 0 and is stronger than the cited statement.","context_sha256":"99298b082510cf73937a325f565a43c0e2c23b6a86376c50f2fda33a36ecf630","at":"2026-08-03T07:29:07.701Z"}
research/audit/wave1b-judge-paired.jsonl:139:{"id":"cor-of-reverse-triangle","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","keep":false,"reason":"Fact [L2] claims that lem-of-abs-value states '|w| equals w or -w' but the lemma's statement does not contain that clause. This is a stronger claim than the cited item.","context_sha256":"ad3986472bba0b894215140184a158e54d5a686efc7a3dfd4de71c5eb340a53d","at":"2026-08-03T07:29:34.928Z"}
research/audit/wave1b-judge-paired.jsonl:141:{"id":"lem-of-naturals-positive","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":true,"reason":"Verified the induction, adjacent strict inequalities, injectivity, and additive and multiplicative identities from the stated recursion and ordered-field facts.","context_sha256":"c3cdb0ec6b6128d50102b70037006a3e63de1cd9f7b6f06eb429a72132ade2a8","at":"2026-08-03T07:29:43.613Z"}
research/audit/wave1b-judge-paired.jsonl:142:{"id":"cor-archimedean-reciprocal","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":false,"reason":"Step 3.1 infers 0 < n times 1_F by transitivity from the preceding inequalities, but its cited facts only provide trichotomy and field inverses. No cited fact establishes order transitivity for this move.","context_sha256":"2cde755a12c585dcef9c161154ecec23422f24c28b130ec0b520743983725267","at":"2026-08-03T07:29:51.160Z"}
research/audit/wave1b-judge-paired.jsonl:144:{"id":"lem-of-inverse-positive","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","keep":true,"reason":"Every step is correctly justified by the cited facts: part 1 uses trichotomy and sign rules, part 2 uses transitivity and the positive multiplier a^{-1}b^{-1}. No logical gaps or mis-citations.","context_sha256":"f69074eeab2079cb28440f073ea05766789e54af66c0e0869d9c50e91514926a","at":"2026-08-03T07:29:56.893Z"}
research/audit/wave1b-judge-paired.jsonl:145:{"id":"thm-of-archimedean","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":true,"reason":"Verified the supremum contradiction and the cited facts faithfully support the canonical-natural and completeness steps.","context_sha256":"771fa4542e89f948569d6009c82eb2c5fa8ca289f81763c9abfc7ec2446d4700","at":"2026-08-03T07:29:58.892Z"}
research/audit/wave1b-judge-paired.jsonl:147:{"id":"lem-of-q-embeds","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":false,"reason":"Fact L1 inaccurately attributes the numerator sign criterion for a rational p over q to thm-rat-ordered-field. The supplied theorem only states that the rationals form a totally ordered field; it does not state that criterion.","context_sha256":"5cd71af83699cc3309f1e4e7bd9f5e4d205befab7a6700c6ca8eb8f0a6ec4167","at":"2026-08-03T07:30:04.042Z"}
research/audit/wave1b-judge-paired.jsonl:148:{"id":"lem-of-abs-value","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","keep":true,"reason":"All steps are logically justified by the cited facts; cases exhaust possibilities; each claimed property is established; no missing citations or logical gaps.","context_sha256":"aecd5d16dbeb1e08aaa7799ea77b6647a9b62c1494a809c837945b274fdb998a","at":"2026-08-03T07:30:09.466Z"}
research/audit/wave1b-judge-paired.jsonl:163:{"id":"thm-of-archimedean","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","keep":true,"reason":"Proof valid: assuming not Archimedean, canonical naturals are bounded above, supremum exists by completeness, subtracting 1 yields a contradiction. Steps correctly cite facts [L1]-[L3] which faithfully restate their sources.","context_sha256":"771fa4542e89f948569d6009c82eb2c5fa8ca289f81763c9abfc7ec2446d4700","at":"2026-08-03T07:31:36.402Z"}
research/audit/wave1b-judge-paired.jsonl:169:{"id":"lem-of-naturals-positive","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","keep":true,"reason":"The proof correctly establishes all stated properties using induction and the cited facts. [L1] and [L2] faithfully represent the cited items, and each step is licensed by the given recursion, the field axioms, and these facts. No logical gaps or mis-citations were found.","context_sha256":"c3cdb0ec6b6128d50102b70037006a3e63de1cd9f7b6f06eb429a72132ade2a8","at":"2026-08-03T07:32:17.839Z"}
research/audit/wave1b-judge-paired.jsonl:171:{"id":"lem-of-square-monotone","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","keep":false,"reason":"Fact [L3] claims |x|^2 = x^2 from lem-of-abs-value, but that lemma does not state this; it only gives |x|>=0 and multiplicativity. Step 5.1 uses the unreferenced equality, lacking justification. Missing dependency on lem-of-square-positive.","context_sha256":"3d586103fac8c461de2b0a3393bceab0298605f86e8a5179b42eb32575b75633","at":"2026-08-03T07:32:42.914Z"}
research/audit/wave1b-judge-paired.jsonl:183:{"id":"lem-of-q-embeds","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","keep":false,"reason":"Fact [L1] states a nonzero p/q with q≥1 is positive iff p≥1, citing thm-rat-ordered-field. That theorem does not assert this; the property comes from def-rat-order, which is not cited. The proof depends on this uncited fact, so the argument is incomplete.","context_sha256":"5cd71af83699cc3309f1e4e7bd9f5e4d205befab7a6700c6ca8eb8f0a6ec4167","at":"2026-08-03T07:33:39.802Z"}
research/audit/wave1b-judge-paired.jsonl:201:{"id":"thm-metric-completion-unique","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":false,"reason":"[L5] cites lem-of-abs-value for the triangle inequality of absolute value, but that cited item states no such inequality. Thus its derivation of the quadrilateral estimate is not licensed by the facts it names.","context_sha256":"99698ebdc071c610f29ae01a2a35c2ab0559da6ea652605539bd5959413dd500","at":"2026-08-03T07:35:25.106Z"}
research/audit/wave1b-judge-paired.jsonl:205:{"id":"thm-metric-completion-exists","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":false,"reason":"Fact L1 cites lem-of-abs-value for the triangle inequality of absolute value, but that cited lemma does not state it. Its claimed derivation of the quadrilateral estimate is therefore not licensed by the cited facts.","context_sha256":"113e7c0d871a9a1799a91785401250777da405c2a1b01328793e1f44de06e4d7","at":"2026-08-03T07:35:51.923Z"}
research/audit/wave1b-judge-paired.jsonl:206:{"id":"cor-archimedean-reciprocal","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","keep":true,"reason":"Proof correctly applies Archimedean property to the inverse of epsilon and uses inversion monotonicity to obtain 1/(n·1_F) < epsilon. All citations are accurate and the reasoning is sound.","context_sha256":"2cde755a12c585dcef9c161154ecec23422f24c28b130ec0b520743983725267","at":"2026-08-03T07:36:05.806Z"}
research/audit/wave1b-judge-paired.jsonl:209:{"id":"lem-complete-remetrisation","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":false,"reason":"L5 falsely attributes the triangle inequality for absolute value to lem-of-abs-value; the cited statement lists no such inequality. Step 1.3 relies on that unsupported assertion to make sigma a metric.","context_sha256":"df48f1ef19e275cc4a86b09280f9f5e5a713e5b26cf509472d5314554841740c","at":"2026-08-03T07:36:17.639Z"}
research/audit/wave1b-judge-paired.jsonl:250:{"id":"lem-of-triangle-inequality","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","keep":false,"reason":"[L2] restates lem-of-add-order with a nonstrict addition rule the lemma does not prove; [L3] cites def-ordered-field for properties it does not state. The proof depends on these overstatements.","context_sha256":"39a55dd1003fe17cd4c532d8c78272e493abaf9df1765adf95b69d6439a492ae","at":"2026-08-03T07:40:23.222Z"}
research/audit/wave1b-judge-paired.jsonl:262:{"id":"lem-complete-remetrisation","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","keep":false,"reason":"L5 claims lem-of-abs-value states the absolute value satisfies the triangle inequality, but the supplied text does not include that property. Step 1.3 then uses L5 to justify that sigma is a metric, making that step unsupported.","context_sha256":"df48f1ef19e275cc4a86b09280f9f5e5a713e5b26cf509472d5314554841740c","at":"2026-08-03T07:41:05.262Z"}
research/audit/wave1b-judge-paired.jsonl:266:{"id":"ex-sqrt-two-exists","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","keep":true,"reason":"The proof correctly applies thm-of-square-roots (L1) and lem-of-q-embeds (L2), and uses the known fact that no rational squares to 2 (L3) to show irrationality. All steps are licensed by the cited items; no logical gaps or misstatements found.","context_sha256":"015e40e85f8d7f7ca6282d30c480cf53a720e1df677f8271e23b28937d23d2e5","at":"2026-08-03T07:41:32.221Z"}
