research/frontier-5-judge.jsonl:46:{"id":"thm-tauber-converse-for-abel-summability","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":false,"reason":"[L2] overstates [[cor-archimedean-reciprocal]]. Its statement gives only one n with 1/n<ε; its remarks explicitly leave the eventual monotonicity argument to the caller. No monotonicity fact or derivation establishes 1/ι(N+1)→0 (hence x_N↑1).","context_sha256":"54d78d06efac2f422b0f1e7374b78b68de3d1c2ea01c8ac4883a5f8f000cbdd2","at":"2026-07-31T11:51:03.093Z"}
research/frontier-5-judge.jsonl:102:{"id":"lem-abel-transform-of-cesaro-means","model":"gpt-5.6-terra","keep":false,"reason":"Step 1.1 applies [L4] but never establishes that \\(M\\iota(n+1)x^n\\ge0\\). Neither [L2] nor [L1]'s cited canonical-natural definition states \\(\\iota(n+1)>0\\); that definition explicitly defers positivity to lem-of-naturals-positive.","context_sha256":"ac30c2a66cb83294fef1a004ea68fdabc16a801f24b8b421dca7b5a053a64cfc","at":"2026-07-31T12:27:55.290Z"}
