research/audit/wave4-dispatch/certifier-certify-ra.log:6399:**Given:** The constant sequence $x_k := 0$ and the sequence $y_k := \bigl((k+1) \cdot 1_{\mathbb{R}}\bigr)^{-1}$, where $n \cdot 1_{\mathbb{R}}$ denotes the canonical natural of $\mathbb{R}$ ([[lem-of-naturals-positive]], [[def-sequence]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/certifier-certify-ra.log:6403:[L2] Archimedean property: for every $z \in \mathbb{R}$ there is a natural $N \ge 1$ with $z < N \cdot 1_{\mathbb{R}}$ ([[thm-of-archimedean]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/certifier-certify-ra.log:6405:[L3] Canonical naturals: $n \cdot 1_{\mathbb{R}} > 0$ for every $n \ge 1$, and $n \mapsto n \cdot 1_{\mathbb{R}}$ is strictly increasing on $\{1, 2, 3, \dots\}$ ([[lem-of-naturals-positive]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/certifier-certify-ra.log:6407:[L4] Inverses and order: $a > 0$ implies $a^{-1} > 0$; $0 < a < b$ implies $0 < b^{-1} < a^{-1}$; and $(u^{-1})^{-1} = u$ for $u \ne 0$ ([[lem-of-inverse-positive]], [[def-field]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/certifier-certify-ra.log:6409:[L5] Absolute value: $|u| = u$ when $u \ge 0$, and $|u - 0| = |u|$ ([[lem-of-abs-value]], [[def-real-order]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/certifier-certify-ra.log:6437:- The sequence $1/(k+1)$ used here is the standard witness that the Archimedean property is what makes $\mathbb{R}$ have no infinitesimals ([[thm-of-archimedean]]); by [[lem-reciprocal-of-null-diverges]] its reciprocals diverge to $+\infty$.
