research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-t4-local-baire-onepoint.log:6516:items/cex-projection-is-not-closed.md:74:[L1] The multiplication map $m : \mathbb{R}^2 \to \mathbb{R}$, $m(x,y) := xy$, is continuous. At $(a,b)$ and for $\varepsilon > 0$, take $$\delta := \min\left\{1,\ \frac{\varepsilon}{|a|+|b|+1}\right\}>0.$$ If $d_\infty((x,y),(a,b))<\delta$, then $|x|<|a|+1$ and $$|xy-ab|\le |x|\,|y-b|+|b|\,|x-a| < (|a|+|b|+1)\delta\le\varepsilon.$$ The bound uses $xy-ab = x(y-b)+b(x-a)$, the triangle inequality $|u+v|\le|u|+|v|$ ([[lem-of-triangle-inequality]]) and $|uv|=|u|\,|v|$ ([[lem-of-abs-value]]). This is the metric definition of continuity ([[def-metric-continuity]], [[lem-of-inverse-positive]], [[def-max-min]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-t4-local-baire-onepoint.log:6525:items/fs-projections-are-closed-maps.md:68:[L1] The multiplication map $m : \mathbb{R}^2 \to \mathbb{R}$, $m(x,y) := xy$, is continuous. Indeed, at $(a,b)$ and for $\varepsilon > 0$, put $$\delta := \min\left\{1,\ \frac{\varepsilon}{|a|+|b|+1}\right\}>0.$$ If $d_\infty((x,y),(a,b))<\delta$, then $|x|<|a|+1$ and $$|xy-ab|\le |x|\,|y-b|+|b|\,|x-a| < (|a|+|b|+1)\delta\le\varepsilon.$$ The bound uses $xy-ab = x(y-b)+b(x-a)$, the triangle inequality $|u+v|\le|u|+|v|$ ([[lem-of-triangle-inequality]]) and $|uv|=|u|\,|v|$ ([[lem-of-abs-value]]). This is the metric definition of continuity ([[def-metric-continuity]], [[lem-of-inverse-positive]], [[def-max-min]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/certifier-certify-f-examples.result.json:16:  "tail": "COLLATERAL: none found\nSTAMPS: verification contains only precheck: pass. No judge, verified, or audited stamp survives; this is correct after the material repair.\n\n### ex-the-cardinality-of-the-continuum — REFUSE\nCURRENT TEXT READ: \"[L7] For a well-orderable set $X$, $\\lvert X\\rvert$ is the least ordinal equinumerous with $X$ and equinumerous sets receive the same one ([[lem-cardinality-of-a-well-orderable-set]], [[def-cardinal]]); assuming the Axiom of Choice every set has one ([[thm-well-ordering-theorem]]).\" / \"[L1] $\\mathbb{R}$ is a complete ordered field with a total order ([[def-real-numbers]], [[def-complete-ordered-field]], [[def-real-order]]), hence Archimedean ([[thm-of-archimedean]]), and $\\iota : \\mathbb{Q} \\to \\mathbb{R}$ is the unique order-preserving field embedding ([[lem-of-q-embeds]]).\"\nASSESSMENT: The L7 repair is correct: lem-cardinality-of-a-well-orderable-set gives the least equinumerous ordinal for a well-orderable set, def-cardinal defines the resulting initial ordinal, and thm-well-ordering-theorem says “Assume the Axiom of Choice. Then every set X can be well ordered.” But L1 remains a fatal dependency-citation defect. def-real-numbers says only “The real numbers are the quotient ring” of Cauchy sequences by null sequences. def-real-order defines positivity and the relation. def-complete-ordered-field defines what completeness means for an already ordered field. None states that this constructed real system is totally ordered or complete. The missing targets state exactly what is needed: thm-reals-ordered-field says the published relation “makes R a totally ordered field,” and cor-cauchy-reals-lub-complete says the Cauchy-sequence reals “have the least-upper-bound property.” Since thm-of-archimedean assumes a complete ordered field, it cannot supply its own unmet hypothesis. Thus L1 and its uses are not licensed by the declared dependencies.\nCOLLATERAL: the L7 repair itself broke nothing; the separate load-bearing L1 citation defect remains unresolved\nSTAMPS: verification contains only precheck: pass. No stale judge, verified, or audited stamp survives; that unstamped state is honest, but certification is refused.\n\n### ex-the-cofinality-of-aleph-omega — CERTIFY\nCURRENT TEXT READ: \"[L5] For a well-orderable set $X$, $\\lvert X\\rvert$ is the least ordinal equinumerous with $X$, and equinumerous sets receive the same one ([[lem-cardinality-of-a-well-orderable-set]], [[def-equinumerous]]).\" / \"[L6] Ordinals satisfy trichotomy, $\\alpha \\subseteq \\beta$ iff $\\alpha \\in \\beta$ or $\\alpha = \\beta$, and $\\alpha \\subseteq \\beta \\subseteq \\alpha$ forces $\\alpha = \\beta$ ([[lem-ordinal-trichotomy]], [[lem-ordinal-basics]]).\"\nASSESSMENT: Correct. lem-cardinality-of-a-well-orderable-set says that a well-orderable X has a least equinumerous ordinal and that equinumerous well-orderable sets receive the same cardinal; def-equinumerous says equinumerous means that a bijection exists. lem-ordinal-trichotomy says exactly one membership direction or equality holds, while lem-ordinal-basics states the equivalence between ordinal inclusion and membership-or-equality. These license L5 and L6. Removing the injection-definition citation was correct because L6 uses only ordinal comparison. The range of the strictly increasing map from omega is cofinal, has cardinality aleph zero, and the lower bound follows from cofinality being an infinite cardinal.\nCOLLATERAL: none found\nSTAMPS: verification contains only precheck: pass. No judge, verified, or audited stamp survives; this is correct after the material repair.\n\n### ex-a-singular-cardinal-of-uncountable-cofinality — CERTIFY\nCURRENT TEXT READ: \"[L7] For a well-orderable set $X$, $\\lvert X\\rvert$ is the least ordinal equinumerous with $X$, equinumerous sets receive the same one, and $\\lvert \\alpha\\rvert = \\alpha$ exactly when $\\alpha$ is a cardinal ([[lem-cardinality-of-a-well-orderable-set]], [[def-cardinal]], [[def-equinumerous]]).\" / \"[L9] Ordinals satisfy trichotomy; $\\alpha \\subseteq \\beta$ iff $\\alpha \\in \\beta$ or $\\alpha = \\beta$; the union of a set of ordinals is its least upper bound; every nonempty set of ordinals has an $\\in$-least element; and every strictly increasing map of ordinals is injective ([[lem-ordinal-trichotomy]], [[lem-ordinal-basics]], [[def-injection-surjection-bijection]]).\"\nASSESSMENT: Correct. The cardinality lemma gives the least equinumerous ordinal, invariance under equinumerosity, and the exact cardinal criterion; def-cardinal and def-equinumerous supply those terms. lem-ordinal-trichotomy gives trichotomy and least elements, lem-ordinal-basics gives the union and inclusion clauses, and def-injection-surjection-bijection says a map is injective when equality of values forces equality of inputs. Strict increase therefore implies injectivity in one line. The lower-bound argument is valid: thm-countable-subsets-of-omega-one-are-bounded says, under countable choice, every at-most-countable subset of omega one is bounded there; thm-cofinality-basics says cofinality of a limit ordinal is an infinite cardinal. These yield cofinality exactly aleph one.\nCOLLATERAL: none found\nSTAMPS: verification contains only precheck: pass. No judge, verified, or audited stamp survives; this is correct after the material repair.\n\n### ex-an-aleph-fixed-point — CERTIFY\nCURRENT TEXT READ: \"The power operation behaves differently: assuming the Axiom of Choice, so that $2^{\\kappa}$ is a cardinal at all, $\\kappa < 2^{\\kappa}$ at every cardinal ([[thm-cardinal-power-set-and-cantor]]), so there are no fixed points there at all. That comparison is an aside; nothing below uses it, and the example itself stays in ZF.\" / \"[L7] An injective map onto its range is a bijection to that range; for a well-orderable set $X$, $\\lvert X\\rvert$ is the least ordinal equinumerous with $X$, and equinumerous sets receive the same cardinal ([[def-injection-surjection-bijection]], [[lem-cardinality-of-a-well-orderable-set]], [[def-equinumerous]]).\" / \"So this fixed point is singular, and, assuming the Axiom of Choice, by [[cor-cofinality-of-a-cardinal-power]] it is therefore not a possible value of $2^{\\aleph_0}$.\"\nASSESSMENT: Correct. thm-cardinal-power-set-and-cantor begins “Assume the Axiom of Choice” and states that every cardinal is strictly below its power-set cardinal. cor-cofinality-of-a-cardinal-power also begins with that hypothesis and states that the cofinality of the continuum is greater than aleph zero. Both repaired qualifications are therefore exact. def-injection-surjection-bijection defines injectivity and surjectivity, so an injective map viewed with its range as codomain is immediately bijective; the cardinality lemma then supplies the cardinal of that range. The tower is strictly increasing, its supremum is a limit, continuity gives the fixed-point equation, and its countable cofinal range gives cofinality aleph zero.\nCOLLATERAL: none found; the power-set comparisons are expressly non-load-bearing asides, and every dependency used by the fixed-point proof remains declared\nSTAMPS: verification contains only precheck: pass. No judge, verified, or audited stamp survives; this is correct after the material repair.\n\n### ex-the-beth-hierarchy-computed — CERTIFY\nCURRENT TEXT READ: \"title: \\\"Assuming the Axiom of Choice: $\\\\\\\\beth_0 = \\\\\\\\aleph_0$, $\\\\\\\\beth_1 = 2^{\\\\\\\\aleph_0} = \\\\\\\\lvert \\\\\\\\mathbb{R} \\\\\\\\rvert$, $\\\\\\\\beth_2 = \\\\\\\\lvert \\\\\\\\mathcal{P}(\\\\\\\\mathbb{R}) \\\\\\\\rvert$, and $\\\\\\\\beth_\\\\\\\\omega$ has cofinality $\\\\\\\\aleph_0$\\\"\" / \"[L4] For a well-orderable set $X$, $\\lvert X\\rvert$ is the least ordinal equinumerous with $X$, equinumerous sets receive the same one, and $\\lvert \\alpha\\rvert = \\alpha$ exactly when $\\alpha$ is a cardinal ([[lem-cardinality-of-a-well-orderable-set]], [[def-cardinal]], [[def-equinumerous]]); assuming the Axiom of Choice every set has a cardinality ([[thm-well-ordering-theorem]]).\" / \"[L7] $\\omega$ is a limit ordinal; ordinals satisfy trichotomy, the union of a set of ordinals is its least upper bound, $\\alpha \\subseteq \\beta$ iff $\\alpha \\in \\beta$ or $\\alpha = \\beta$, and every strictly increasing map of ordinals is injective ([[lem-omega-least-limit-ordinal]], [[lem-ordinal-basics]], [[lem-ordinal-trichotomy]], [[def-injection-surjection-bijection]]).\"\nASSESSMENT: Correct. def-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies says “The beths, assuming the Axiom of Choice, are the parallel operation” and gives the base, successor, and limit clauses; the hierarchy corollary gives infinite cardinal values, strict increase, and continuity. The repaired title now matches that hypothesis. The cardinality lemma, def-cardinal, and def-equinumerous license L4, while thm-well-ordering-theorem says every set can be well ordered under choice. The omega lemma says omega is a limit ordinal; the ordinal lemmas give trichotomy, unions, and comparison; the injection definition makes strict increase imply injectivity immediately. The first three beth values and the cofinality calculation follow correctly.\nCOLLATERAL: none found\nSTAMPS: verification contains only precheck: pass. No judge, verified, or audited stamp survives; this is correct after the material repair.\n\n### ex-counting-functions-and-subsets-of-the-continuum — CERTIFY\nCURRENT TEXT READ: \"title: \\\"Assuming the Axiom of Choice: $\\\\\\\\aleph_0^{\\\\\\\\aleph_0} = 2^{\\\\\\\\aleph_0}$ and $\\\\\\\\lvert \\\\\\\\mathbb{R}^{\\\\\\\\mathbb{R}} \\\\\\\\rvert = 2^{2^{\\\\\\\\aleph_0}}$, computed from the exponent laws and Hessenberg\\\"\" / \"[L7] Ordinals satisfy trichotomy, $\\alpha \\subseteq \\beta$ iff $\\alpha \\in \\beta$ or $\\alpha = \\beta$, and $\\alpha \\subseteq \\beta \\subseteq \\alpha$ forces $\\alpha = \\beta$ ([[lem-ordinal-trichotomy]], [[lem-ordinal-basics]]).\"\nASSESSMENT: Correct. def-cardinal-arithmetic says that, assuming the Axiom of Choice, every function set is well-orderable and cardinal exponentiation is defined for all cardinals; thm-well-ordering-theorem says every set can then be well ordered. The repaired title therefore states the proof’s actual hypothesis. lem-ordinal-trichotomy and lem-ordinal-basics supply exactly the comparison and inclusion facts in L7, so removing the irrelevant injection-definition citation was correct. lem-cardinal-arithmetic-basic-laws states base monotonicity and the iterated-exponent law; thm-hessenberg states that an infinite cardinal multiplied by itself equals itself; cor-cardinal-absorption supplies the mixed-product collapse. These license both displayed computations.\nCOLLATERAL: none found\nSTAMPS: verification contains only precheck: pass. No judge, verified, or audited stamp survives; this is correct after the material repair.\n\n7 certified, 1 refused"
